description:
Get Google Analytics 4 metrics per individual page (landing/URL) for a property, ranked so you can see which pages drive the most sessions, signups (conversions) or users. The page dimension is the GA4 page path. Each row returns the page plus sessions, users, conversions and engagement_rate (engaged sessions / sessions), each with the immediately preceding period (prev) and change_pct for period-over-period comparison. Accepts a date range as presets (last_7_days, last_28_days, last_3_months, last_year) or absolute dates (from/to in Y-m-d). Sort with sortBy = sessions (default), conversions or users; rows are capped by limit (default 25, max 100). `data_synced` is false when the property has no synced GA4 data yet (so an all-zero result is not mistaken for real zeros), and `data_start_date` is the earliest synced day — `partial_coverage.current` / `partial_coverage.previous` flag when a period starts before it, so the zeros and change_pct for that period are a coverage gap rather than a trend. Note: crossing pages with a traffic source/channel, and new_users / avg_session_duration per page, are not yet available. Pass the project ID (UUID) or URL from list_ga4_properties.

Cost: 5 credits per call.

Examples:
```json
// Top landing pages by GA4 sessions for the last 28 days vs the prior period.
{"property":"sc-domain:example.com","range":"last_28_days"}

// Top 10 pages by conversions (signups) over the last 3 months.
{"property":"sc-domain:example.com","range":"last_3_months","sortBy":"conversions","limit":10}
```
